Good morning,

There is currently drilling which is preventing me access and also welding =
that produces a hazardous environment. Although the construction workers ar=
e using gear and appear to be following healthy work and safety protocol wh=
at about the effects on my health? The noise is above 120 dc and there are =
toxic fumes being produced although the windows are opened a crack. How can=
 I do my laundry or use my storage unit when this is underway? Notice in th=
e video the inaccessibility.

The measurements of the storage unit are 90 cm x 60 cm x 60 cm. The door is=
 unlocked from 8:30 am until 4:30 pm each day of construction.

Please note that on form 8 the landlord has stated there will be no rent re=
duction despite stating otherwise in emails to me. I assume you have access=
 to a copy.

Mr. Maclean, this landlord has engaged in deceptive practices and the reaso=
ns are clear: Although the laundry and storage services have been provided =
to me since my tenancy began in 2012, new tenants have not had the services=
 indicated in their lease agreements. The service of storage was denied to =
new tenants without following proper protocol because the landlord has had =
plans to do this two suite creation since 2018 upon purchase of the propert=
y. Despite having the storage units available and identified as correlated =
to individual suites (see photos in previous emails) the landlord has left =
these services empty and were not provided to tenants at no cost to themsel=
ves and with only the goal of making these renovations as cheap as possible=
 for themselves. Good business practices would be to withdraw the services =
which are a physical reality by following RTB protocol which was not done. =
 The tenants who have either permitted or been deceived into permitting on =
suite renovations in which their storage space was reduced further to make =
room for the laundry services. The fact of the matter is that storage space=
 in each of the renovated units has been decreased and each of the tenants =
since 2018 have been denied the storage unit services despite being availab=
le, accessible, and clearly indicated as correlated to the tenant suites. T=
horwin Properties has engaged is deception and unethical treatment of their=
 tenants and all tenants affected should be reimbursed for these self-servi=
ng practices. Let me be clear, there have been a reduction in services prov=
ided to all tenants and yet rent increases have increased each year which h=
ave deceptively not reflected the reduction in storage space in each of the=
 renovated tenants suites due to the laundry services being installed and d=
enial of storage unit services despite availability and accessibility.

This company has exploited RTB protocol on technicality and this cannot be =
allowed.

When you determine the amount of rent decrease that the withdrawal of servi=
ce of my unit will result in monthly I have an additional request:

Each of the tenants since 2018 have had access denied to services that have=
 been clearly identified on each of the now destructed storage units. I wan=
t the RTB to recognize that service withdrawal protocol was not followed by=
 Thorwin, each of tenants should have had access to the associated storage =
units as I have, and it would be prudent and just for the RTB to order Thor=
win Properties to retroactively payback the equivalent month by month value=
 of storage fees that are included in the rent amount paid by the tenants f=
rom 2018 onwards.

I look forward to your response.

All the best,
Evan Rosner
